{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE HELP SURFACE'S MASTHEAD — one identity, one search, one row of tabs
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  ── THE FAULT THIS EXISTS TO END ────────────────────────────────────────────

  There were two front doors to the same job. `/help` opened with "What has gone
  wrong?" over a search field; `/support` opened with "We're here to help" over
  four cards, the first of which was "Search the Help Centre → Browse the
  answers" — which lands on `/help`. A stuck person hit a router that routed them
  to another router, and neither page could tell them the other one existed.

  They are one surface now, with the three things a person can actually do side by
  side: read an answer, ask the assistant to fix it, or reach a person. Whichever
  they land on, the other two are one tap away and the search field is the same
  field.

  ── WHY THE IDENTITY LINE SAYS WHOSE HELP THIS IS ───────────────────────────

  Google's support masthead says "Google Account Help", not "Google Help", so a
  reader always knows whose answers they are reading. Ours said nothing at all,
  on a platform where a supporter, a nominee, a judge and a partner organisation
  arrive with almost disjoint problems — and where, until this week, there was
  not one article written for a judge or for an organisation.

  When an audience is chosen the line says so. That is the whole mechanism: it is
  a LABEL and a filter, never a partition. See HelpCentre::AUDIENCES.

  ── THE SEARCH IS IN THE MASTHEAD, SO IT IS ON EVERY TAB ────────────────────

  A real GET form on every surface, not a filter that only exists on the index.
  Somebody reading an answer that turns out to be the wrong answer should not
  have to go back to search again.

  `tab` is 'answers' | 'assistant' | 'contact'.
  `audience` is a HelpCentre audience key, or empty.
#}
{# The surface's own sheet, deliberately outside AssetBundle::STYLESHEETS: it is
   loaded by the six help surfaces and by nothing else, and bundling it into the
   global payload to save a request on those six makes every other page heavier.
   `'self'` in style-src-elem covers it, so no nonce is needed. #}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/help-nav.css') }}">

{% set _tab = tab|default('answers') %}
{% set _aud = audience|default('') %}

<header class="hn">
  <div class="hn__in">
    {# The identity, and the scope when there is one. `aria-current` is on the tab
       row below rather than here: this is a heading, not a control. #}
    <p class="hn__id">
      <a href="/help">Help centre</a>
      {%- set _auds = help_audiences() %}
      {%- if _aud and _auds[_aud] is defined %}
        <span class="hn__scope" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span class="hn__scope">{{ _auds[_aud].title }}</span>
      {%- endif %}
    </p>

    <form class="hn__find" method="get" action="/help" role="search">
      <label class="sr-only" for="hn-q">Search the help centre</label>
      <svg class="hn__mag" width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
           stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5"/>
      </svg>
      {# `search_model` binds this field to the including page's Alpine state, which is
         what lets the answers index narrow as you type without a second search field on
         the page. Absent — every other surface — it is a plain GET input and behaves
         identically with scripting off. #}
      <input id="hn-q" type="search" name="q" value="{{ q|default('') }}"
             {% if search_model|default('') %}x-model="{{ search_model }}"{% endif %}
             placeholder="{{ search_placeholder|default('Describe your problem') }}" autocomplete="off">
      {# The chosen audience rides with the search, so a nominee who searches stays a
         nominee. It is a filter on the shelf and never on the results — see
         HelpCentre::search(), which ignores it outright. #}
      {% if _aud %}<input type="hidden" name="for" value="{{ _aud }}">{% endif %}
      <button type="submit">Search</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  {#
    THE THREE THINGS A STUCK PERSON CAN DO, ALWAYS ALL THREE.

    Ordered by what costs them least: an answer is instant, the assistant can fix a
    payment without waiting for anyone, a person takes until the next working day.
    Nobody should reach the third without having been shown the first two, and
    nobody should be unable to reach the third from the first.
  #}
  <nav class="hn__tabs" aria-label="Help">
    <a href="/help{{ _aud ? '?for=' ~ _aud : '' }}"
       {% if _tab == 'answers' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Answers</a>
    <a href="/support/assistant"
       {% if _tab == 'assistant' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Ask the assistant</a>
    <a href="/support"
       {% if _tab == 'contact' %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Contact us</a>
  </nav>
</header>
